WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.139 --> 00:00:05.540
When dealing with a lot of assets inside of your level,

2
00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:08.580
there are two things that can become an issue.

3
00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:12.220
The first is just dealing with that amount of data.

4
00:00:12.220 --> 00:00:14.179
Well, oftentimes, level builders

5
00:00:14.179 --> 00:00:16.660
will use a method called kitbashing,

6
00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:19.339
which means taking a few different types of static

7
00:00:19.339 --> 00:00:22.300
meshes and moving them together in interesting ways

8
00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:25.079
to create other types of assets.

9
00:00:25.079 --> 00:00:27.500
And we can see that in this example here.

10
00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:29.699
Here, we've taken these sandstone rocks

11
00:00:29.699 --> 00:00:31.660
and arranged them to make something

12
00:00:31.660 --> 00:00:34.179
that is a little bit larger and just a little bit easier

13
00:00:34.179 --> 00:00:35.780
to place inside of the level.

14
00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:39.219
Now, we could go about inside of Unreal grouping these.

15
00:00:39.219 --> 00:00:42.700
But this is just a little bit of a problem

16
00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:44.340
because when we group something,

17
00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:45.659
it's specific to that level.

18
00:00:45.659 --> 00:00:47.899
So we can't add it easily to other levels.

19
00:00:47.899 --> 00:00:49.460
We could always copy and paste.

20
00:00:49.460 --> 00:00:53.020
But again, this is kind of workflow intensive.

21
00:00:53.020 --> 00:00:55.460
And we have a great solution for that anyway,

22
00:00:55.460 --> 00:00:58.740
something called a Packed Level Instance Blueprint.

23
00:00:58.740 --> 00:01:01.380
What this is is basically creating a prefab

24
00:01:01.380 --> 00:01:03.740
that you can manipulate out of the actors

25
00:01:03.740 --> 00:01:05.019
that you have selected.

26
00:01:05.019 --> 00:01:07.900
Let's pop over to the editor and see how we do this.

27
00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:10.099
So here, we have some granite cliffs.

28
00:01:10.099 --> 00:01:12.980
I'm just going to hit Shift-E to select all of these.

29
00:01:12.980 --> 00:01:17.900
And I have 114 selected.

30
00:01:17.900 --> 00:01:22.459
Now, if I right-click on this and I go to Level,

31
00:01:22.459 --> 00:01:25.739
there is my Create Packed Level Actor.

32
00:01:25.739 --> 00:01:28.659
So I'm going to just have the default settings.

33
00:01:28.659 --> 00:01:30.219
I'm going to press OK.

34
00:01:30.219 --> 00:01:36.260
New Map, we're going to call this Lifts.

35
00:01:36.260 --> 00:01:39.980
And then we'll just call this BPV for Blueprint Packed.

36
00:01:39.980 --> 00:01:42.120
And then we'll hit Save.

37
00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:45.799
And what's going to happen is now I will have that.

38
00:01:45.799 --> 00:01:48.359
And you can see here, it's been changed to just this one

39
00:01:48.359 --> 00:01:48.840
asset.

40
00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:51.319
But if I come into my Content Browser, boom, look at that.

41
00:01:51.319 --> 00:01:53.159
I have just created something else

42
00:01:53.159 --> 00:01:57.079
that I can pull out and easily put into any level

43
00:01:57.079 --> 00:01:58.359
to manipulate.

44
00:01:58.400 --> 00:02:01.480
Maybe if I flip this upside down 180 degrees,

45
00:02:01.480 --> 00:02:04.560
we'll get some completely different-looking rocks.

46
00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:07.959
And again, if I was to come up here to File, New Level,

47
00:02:07.959 --> 00:02:11.319
just going to select the empty open world and hit Create.

48
00:02:11.319 --> 00:02:13.879
I'm not going to save this and just give this a second

49
00:02:13.879 --> 00:02:14.400
to open up.

50
00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:16.439
Let's hit 1 to get down to the ground.

51
00:02:16.439 --> 00:02:18.280
And then we're going to pull this back in.

52
00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:18.840
Look at that.

53
00:02:18.840 --> 00:02:22.039
I've got this BP Cliffs that I can just quickly and easily

54
00:02:22.039 --> 00:02:22.680
add.

55
00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:25.560
Now, if that wasn't cool enough, check this out.

56
00:02:25.599 --> 00:02:29.479
If I want to, I can always right click on this.

57
00:02:29.479 --> 00:02:34.199
And if we go to Level, we can do things like Edit.

58
00:02:34.199 --> 00:02:37.120
So I can actually edit this, which

59
00:02:37.120 --> 00:02:38.939
means I can move things around.

60
00:02:38.939 --> 00:02:40.919
I can add additional ones.

61
00:02:40.919 --> 00:02:42.000
I could delete them.

62
00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:43.599
I can even change their properties,

63
00:02:43.599 --> 00:02:44.840
like their materials.

64
00:02:44.840 --> 00:02:46.479
When I'm done, I just click Exit.

65
00:02:46.479 --> 00:02:49.360
And it's going to automatically update that for me.

66
00:02:49.360 --> 00:02:52.039
So again, I have the full ability.

67
00:02:52.039 --> 00:02:53.800
Again, if I right click, go to my level,

68
00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:56.439
I can also break it apart and edit.

69
00:02:56.439 --> 00:02:58.759
Or I can update the packed level Blueprint

70
00:02:58.759 --> 00:03:00.560
to update other instances in the level.

71
00:03:00.560 --> 00:03:02.060
And that's why this is so powerful,

72
00:03:02.060 --> 00:03:05.520
is it allows us to have a very, very easy to use

73
00:03:05.520 --> 00:03:09.819
prefab that we can then move around and share.

74
00:03:09.819 --> 00:03:11.620
One of the last things I also want to note

75
00:03:11.620 --> 00:03:14.259
is if we check out what this has actually done,

76
00:03:14.259 --> 00:03:19.930
it's created this out of hierarchical instance static

77
00:03:19.930 --> 00:03:20.409
meshes.

78
00:03:20.409 --> 00:03:23.370
So instead of having just one static mesh that's

79
00:03:23.370 --> 00:03:25.250
going to be drawn again and again and again,

80
00:03:25.250 --> 00:03:26.969
we actually have some instances there

81
00:03:26.969 --> 00:03:29.810
so we can take advantage of all of the performance

82
00:03:29.810 --> 00:03:32.409
benefits that that gives us by using

83
00:03:32.409 --> 00:03:35.169
these packed level instances.
